  "comments": [
    {
      "texts": [
        {
          "value": "Electron carrier protein. The oxidized form of the cytochrome c heme group can accept an electron from the heme group of the cytochrome c1 subunit of cytochrome reductase. Cytochrome c then transfers this electron to the cytochrome oxidase complex, the final protein carrier in the mitochondrial electron-transport chain"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "FUNCTION"
    },
    {
      "commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION",
      "note": {
